WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.250
Everything so far stops at
the edge of Microsoft 365.

2
00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:08.934
Nothing on BOD 25-01's list
covers infrastructure accounts,

3
00:00:08.934 --> 00:00:11.900
the agency network or
the virtualized estate.

4
00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:15.599
So the whole-agency argument
rests on the Zero Trust documents,

5
00:00:15.599 --> 00:00:21.787
and on the SP 800-53 controls every
security plan already asserts.

6
00:00:21.787 --> 00:00:24.563
Three things get reconciled
before you assess.

7
00:00:24.563 --> 00:00:27.837
One inventory, with no
component counted twice.

8
00:00:27.837 --> 00:00:33.749
One naming authority, because each cloud
and VMware ships its own private DNS.

9
00:00:33.749 --> 00:00:37.658
And no implicit trust from any
boundary: a site-to-site VPN,

10
00:00:37.658 --> 00:00:43.062
a default virtual network and a flat
virtualized segment are the same mistake.

11
00:00:43.062 --> 00:00:47.168
The hypervisor is its own threat
class, so its management plane

12
00:00:47.168 --> 00:00:51.037
is assessed as its own surface,
not inferred from its guests.

13
00:00:51.037 --> 00:00:54.688
And every provider's tool answers
only for its own platform.

14
00:00:54.688 --> 00:00:56.780
Next, who owns the posture.
